{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018G6Pckjc8iGoHtEJRNYHdz","type":"tool_result","content":"682- * @since 4.0.0\n683- */\n684:export declare const retryTransient: {\n685-    /**\n686-     * Retries common transient errors, such as rate limiting, timeouts or network issues.\n687-     *\n688-     * **When to use**\n689-     *\n690-     * Use to focus on retrying errors, transient responses, or both.\n691-     *\n692-     * **Details**\n693-     *\n694-     * Specifying a `while` predicate allows you to consider other errors as\n695-     * transient, and is ignored in \"response-only\" mode.\n696-     *\n697-     * A `Retry-After` header on a transient response, or on the response of a\n698-     * status code error, sets the minimum delay before the next attempt.\n--\n787- * A timed out request is interrupted and fails with an `HttpClientError` whose\n788- * reason is a `TransportError` with a `Cause.TimeoutError` cause.\n789: * `retryTransient` treats it as transient. Interrupting a request aborts the\n790- * underlying transport, unless the request is attached to a scope with\n791- * `withScope`, in which case it stays open until the scope closes.\n792- *\n793- * The timer starts after request preprocessing and covers everything the\n794- * wrapped client does to produce a response. For a plain client this ends when\n795- * the response headers arrive, but response middleware applied before\n796: * `timeout`, such as `tap` or `retryTransient`, runs inside the budget,\n797- * including any body reads it performs. Composition order therefore decides\n798: * how it interacts with retries: applying `timeout` before `retryTransient`\n799- * gives each attempt its own budget, while applying it after bounds the whole\n800- * retry loop.\n801- *\n802- * **Gotchas**\n803- *\n804- * Body reads outside the timed client are not covered, including those made\n805- * by response middleware applied after `timeout` and by consumers of the\n806- * `HttpClient` service. Apply a separate timeout to body reads such as\n807- * `response.json` or `response.stream` when needed.\n808- *\n809- * **Example** (Timing out each attempt)\n810- *\n811- * ```ts\n812- * import { Effect, Layer } from \"effect\"\n--\n823- * const program = Effect.gen(function*() {\n824- *   const client = (yield* HttpClient.HttpClient).pipe(\n825: *     HttpClient.retryTransient({ times: 3 })\n826- *   )\n827- *   return yield* client.get(\"https://example.com\")\n828- * }).pipe(Effect.provide(TimedHttpClient))\n829- * ```\n830- *\n831- * @stability unstable\n832- * @category error handling\n833- * @since 4.1.0\n834- */\n835-export declare const timeout: {\n836-    /**\n837-     * Fails requests that do not receive a response within the given duration.\n----\n----\n11737: * @see {@link TaggedError} for defining tagged schema-backed error classes\n11814:     * @see {@link TaggedError} for defining tagged schema-backed error classes\n11969: * class NotFound extends Schema.TaggedError<NotFound>()(\"NotFound\", {\n11985:export declare const TaggedError: {\n12000:     * class NotFound extends Schema.TaggedError<NotFound>()(\"NotFound\", {\n----\n110:export declare const layer: Layer.Layer<HttpClient.HttpClient>;\nFetchHttpClient.d.ts\nFetchHttpClient.d.ts.map\nFetchHttpClient.js\nFetchHttpClient.js.map\n----","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8a4e7c3-fea7-4574-8534-08f87d17cbad","uuid":"9aa44a2a-06a8-43fc-8b12-02424048e915","timestamp":"2026-11-09T22:56:58.236Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"682- * @since 4.0.0\n683- */\n684:export declare const retryTransient: {\n685-    /**\n686-     * Retries common transient errors, such as rate limiting, timeouts or network issues.\n687-     *\n688-     * **When to use**\n689-     *\n690-     * Use to focus on retrying errors, transient responses, or both.\n691-     *\n692-     * **Details**\n693-     *\n694-     * Specifying a `while` predicate allows you to consider other errors 