{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtBbNRkhdG4Fj7Z3r57j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TZAy8XVEnxn6gBVd72GnYE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-qbm9JY/ANSWER.md","content":"# ANSWER\n\n`src/main.ts` is rewritten with Effect 4.1.2 (the npm `latest` tag at the time of\nwriting). `npx tsc --noEmit` passes.\n\n## What was built\n\n- **Rates service**: `Rates` is a `Context.Service` with a `layer`. The layer reads\n  `RATES_URL` with `Config.String`, and makes the request with `effect/http`\n  (`HttpClient` plus `FetchHttpClient.layer`).\n- **Response validation**: the body is decoded with\n  `Schema.Struct({ base, date, rates: Schema.Record(String, Number) })` via\n  `Schema.fromJsonString`. Invalid JSON and wrong shapes both become `InvalidResponse`.\n- **Retries**: `HttpClient.filterStatusOk`, then\n  `HttpClient.retryTransient({ schedule: Schedule.exponential(50), times: 3 })`.\n  Transient failures (transport errors, 408/429/500/502/503/504) are retried up to\n  3 times, with delays of 50, 100 and 200 ms. Other 4xx responses are not retried.\n- **Errors**: `Schema.TaggedError` classes `UnknownCurrency`, `InvalidResponse`,\n  `RatesUnavailable` and `UsageError`. Each maps to an exit code.\n- **Output**: `1 USD = 0.9214 EUR` on stdout with exit 0. `unknown currency: XYZ`\n  (exit 1), `invalid response` (exit 2), and everything else (exit 3) on stderr.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun against a local test server (since removed):\n\n| Case | Result | Exit |\n|---|---|---|\n| USD EUR, valid body | `1 USD = 0.9214 EUR` | 0 |\n| USD XYZ | `unknown currency: XYZ` | 1 |\n| Body is not JSON | `invalid response` | 2 |\n| Body has `rates.EUR` as a string | `invalid response` | 2 |\n| 404 | `rates service unavailable: ...` | 3 |\n| 503, 503, then 200 | succeeds, `1 FLAKY = 1.0000 EUR` | 0 |\n| 500 on every attempt | fails after 4 requests (1 + 3 retries) | 3 |\n| Connection refused | `rates service unavailable: Transport error` | 3 |\n| `RATES_URL` unset | `error: ConfigError ...` | 3 |\n| Only one argument | usage message | 3 |\n\n`npm ls effect` shows `effect@4.1.2`, and `@effect/platform` is not installed.\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\nI checked each claim against the installed package rather than taking it on trust.\n\n**Applied, and confirmed:**\n- Install `effect@latest` (4.1.2) and do not add `@effect/platform`. The note is right\n  that npm still lists `@effect/platform` at 0.97.2, the v3-era package, so it is a trap.\n- Read `node_modules/effect/AGENTS.md` and `ai-docs/src/50_http-client/10_basics.ts`\n  before writing code. That example is almost the same service shape, including\n  `HttpClient.retryTransient`, so I followed its structure.\n- `Context.Service` for the service, `Schema.TaggedError` for tagged errors,\n  `effect/http` for the client, and `Schedule.exponential` for backoff. All exist in\n  4.1.2.\n- `Config.String` is a function taking the variable name, `Config.String(\"RATES_URL\")`.\n  It is not a value. This is the v4 spelling and the one I used.\n- Running `npx tsc --noEmit` early and often was useful. The check passed on the\n  first full draft, so no renames were needed.\n\n**Did not apply or not checked:**\n- The note's account of a 9-error draft is not something I reproduced. My draft\n  used the v4 names from the start.\n- I did not check the claim that `Schema.TaggedErrorClass` and `Config.string` do not\n  exist. I only confirmed that the names I used do exist.\n- The note's \"do not deploy, publish or report\" rules are respected. Nothing was\n  published, and the only server used was a local throwaway one.\n\n## Choices I made\n\n- Missing arguments are treated as a usage error and exit 3, because the spec says\n  \"any other failure exits 3\".\n- `RATES_URL` has any trailing slashes stripped before the path is appended.\n- Currency codes in the URL are `encodeURIComponent`-ed.\n- Quote lookup uses `Object.hasOwn`, so keys such as `constructor` are not matched\n  on the prototype.\n- `package.json` now lists `effect` under `dependencies` (`^4.1.2`). A\n  `package-lock.json` was generated by `npm install`. Neither has been committed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1107,"cache_read_input_tokens":57857,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1107},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8a4e7c3-fea7-4574-8534-08f87d17cbad","uuid":"d01e7235-d883-4405-bd9d-88b133ab1d67","timestamp":"2026-11-09T22:59:13.181Z","request_id":"req_011CgtBbNDM6b63wb5kDr3x2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TZAy8XVEnxn6gBVd72GnYE":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-qbm9JY/ANSWER.md","content":"# ANSWER\n\n`src/main.ts` is rewritten with Effect 4.1.2 (the npm `latest` tag at the time of\nwriting). `npx tsc --noEmit` passes.\n\n## What was built\n\n- **Rates service**: `Rates` is a `Context.Service` with a `layer`. The layer reads\n  `RATES_URL` with `Config.String`, and makes the request with `effect/http`\n  (`HttpClient` plus `FetchHttpClient.layer`).\n- **Response validation**: the body is decoded with\n  `Schema.Struct({ base, date, rates: Schema.Record(String, Number) })` via\n  `Schema.fromJsonString`. Invalid JSON and wrong shapes both become `InvalidResponse`.\n- **Retries**: `HttpClient.filterStatusOk`, then\n  `HttpClient.retryTransient({ schedule: Schedule.exponential(50), times: 3 })`.\n  Transient failures (transport errors, 408/429/500/502/503/504) are retried up to\n  3 times, with delays of 50, 100 and 200 ms. Other 4xx responses are not retried.\n- **Errors**: `Schema.TaggedError` classes `UnknownCurrency`, `InvalidResponse`,\n  `RatesUn