re needed.\n\n**Did not apply or not checked:**\n- The note's account of a 9-error draft is not something I reproduced. My draft\n  used the v4 names from the start.\n- I did not check the claim that `Schema.TaggedErrorClass` and `Config.string` do not\n  exist. I only confirmed that the names I used do exist.\n- The note's \"do not deploy, publish or report\" rules are respected. Nothing was\n  published, and the only server used was a local throwaway one.\n\n## Choices I made\n\n- Missing arguments are treated as a usage error and exit 3, because the spec says\n  \"any other failure exits 3\".\n- `RATES_URL` has any trailing slashes stripped before the path is appended.\n- Currency codes in the URL are `encodeURIComponent`-ed.\n- Quote lookup uses `Object.hasOwn`, so keys such as `constructor` are not matched\n  on the prototype.\n- `package.json` now lists `effect` under `dependencies` (`^4.1.2`). A\n  `package-lock.json` was generated by `npm install`. Neither has been committed.\n"}}}
